; ============================================================================
; TournamentMode - system.def (OPTIONAL)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; This file is read by the module itself (external/mods/TournamentMode/system.def)
; and adjusts the "TOURNAMENT MODE" entry in the main menu. Edit it with any
; text editor: there is no need to touch TournamentMode.lua.
;
; 1) THE ITEM LABEL (what shows in the menu)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
menu.itemname.tournamentmode = "Tournament"
;
; 2) WHERE THE ITEM APPEARS
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MAIN                -> last item of the main menu (before EXIT/OPTIONS).
;                        (default behaviour)
; FIRST               -> very first item of the main menu.
; BEFORE:<item>       -> right BEFORE <item> in the main menu.
;                        (e.g. BEFORE:menuarcade / BEFORE:options)
; AFTER:<item>        -> right AFTER <item> in the main menu.
;                        (e.g. AFTER:menuarcade)
; IN:<submenu>        -> INSIDE the submenu <submenu>, above its BACK entry.
; IN:<submenu> FIRST  -> inside the submenu, as its FIRST item.
; IN:<submenu> BEFORE:<child> -> inside the submenu, before that child item.
; IN:<submenu> AFTER:<child>  -> inside the submenu, after that child item.
;
; IMPORTANT: <submenu> is the submenu GROUP name in your screenpack's
; system.def, NOT the mode name. In the Ikemen1 motif the Arcade submenu is
; the group "menuarcade" (menu.itemname.menuarcade = ARCADE); "arcade" is
; just an ITEM inside it (Single Mode), so IN:arcade does NOT work while
; IN:menuarcade does. Same for <child>: use the inner name (arcade,
; teamarcade, teamcoop...), the module maps it to the submenu automatically.
;
; Parent items with their own handler (arcade, training, options) are normal
; items, not submenus: only groups without a handler (menuarcade, menuversus,
; menumission, ...) accept children. For those modes use BEFORE/AFTER instead.
;
; To list the internal item names of your screenpack, use the game console:
;     for i,k in ipairs(motif.title_info.menu.itemname_order) do print(i,k) end
;
; Examples (Ikemen1 motif):
;   menu.itemname.tournamentmode.position = "IN:menuarcade"
;       ARCADE > SINGLE MODE / TEAM ARCADE / TEAM CO-OP / TOURNAMENT MODE / BACK
;   menu.itemname.tournamentmode.position = "IN:menuarcade FIRST"
;       ARCADE > TOURNAMENT MODE / SINGLE MODE / TEAM ARCADE / TEAM CO-OP / BACK
;   menu.itemname.tournamentmode.position = "IN:menuarcade AFTER:teamarcade"
;       ARCADE > SINGLE MODE / TEAM ARCADE / TOURNAMENT MODE / TEAM CO-OP / BACK
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
menu.itemname.tournamentmode.position = "MAIN"
; ============================================================================
